WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.200
The vagus carries many specialised sensory lines.

2
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.780
Some report lung inflation and airway irritants.

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.340
Others report arterial stretch, gut stretch or food.

4
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.300
These signals help control breathing, blood pressure and feeding.

5
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:23.040
So the question is what each population reports, which channel senses force, and

6
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.500
where the signal lands in the brain.

7
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.680
We follow the mouse evidence, from organs to sensory neurons to the brainstem.

8
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:36.403
Start in the gut. In awake mice, activating intestinal stretch afferents labelled

9
00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.923
Oxtr strongly suppressed feeding.

10
00:00:39.823 --> 00:00:44.463
Activating gastric afferents labelled Glp1r suppressed it more weakly.

11
00:00:45.803 --> 00:00:51.803
GPR65 afferents responded to intestinal food, but activating them did not measurably

12
00:00:51.803 --> 00:00:53.823
change feeding in the assays tested.

13
00:00:54.943 --> 00:00:59.443
Chemical signals also reach vagal terminals through hormones released by cells in

14
00:00:59.443 --> 00:01:02.163
the including cholecystokinin.

15
00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.787
Airway populations have different jobs too.

16
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:11.307
In anaesthetized mice, light on P2ry1 afferents suppressed breathing.

17
00:01:12.327 --> 00:01:16.087
Light on Npy2r afferents produced rapid shallow breathing.

18
00:01:17.087 --> 00:01:22.787
Driving P2ry1 afferents also recruited airway defence: closed vocal folds,

19
00:01:23.307 --> 00:01:25.487
swallowing and expiratory reflexes.

20
00:01:26.247 --> 00:01:28.167
Light shows what driving these cells can do.

21
00:01:28.827 --> 00:01:31.127
It does not identify their natural stimulus.

22
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:35.187
Lung inflation can also halt inspiration.

23
00:01:36.227 --> 00:01:41.327
Deleting Piezo2 in adult mouse sensory neurons impaired this inflation reflex.

24
00:01:42.347 --> 00:01:45.187
Arterial pressure sensing needed a combined test.

25
00:01:46.047 --> 00:01:51.867
Deleting both Piezo1 and Piezo2 from nodose and petrosal neurons abolished the

26
00:01:51.867 --> 00:01:55.027
baroreflex, in which rising pressure slows the heart.

27
00:01:55.987 --> 00:01:58.487
Neither single deletion changed it detectably.

28
00:01:59.347 --> 00:02:03.387
This shows a collective channel requirement, not both channels in every neuron.

29
00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.967
Where do these signals land?

30
00:02:06.967 --> 00:02:12.907
Vagal sensory axons primarily reach the nucleus of the solitary tract, or NTS, in

31
00:02:12.907 --> 00:02:16.107
the medulla. The brainstem processes the input.

32
00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:20.627
Jugular afferents take a different route, to the paratrigeminal nucleus.

33
00:02:21.527 --> 00:02:24.267
Some gut afferents also reach the area postrema.

34
00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:28.590
A smaller closing point: a genetic label is a handle.

35
00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:33.550
It does not by itself identify the molecule that senses stretch or food.
